---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How InfraTrove handles tool input, local preferences and hosting requests."
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">Last updated · October 24, 2026</div>
    <h1>Your input stays in your browser.</h1>
    <h2>Tool input and output</h2>
    <p>
      Tools process the text you enter and the results they generate inside your
      browser tab. This release has no server endpoint to receive tool input, no
      input history and no automatic persistence of passwords, text or results.
    </p>
    <h2>Local preferences</h2>
    <p>
      We use localStorage for your selected theme and favorite tool identifiers.
      These values stay in your browser profile. You can remove them by clearing
      site data. The tools still work if this storage is unavailable.
    </p>
    <h2>Scripts and measurement</h2>
    <p>
      This release does not include advertising, analytics, session replay or
      remote error-reporting scripts. Tool pages load no third-party scripts.
      Copying output uses your system clipboard only when you click a copy
      button. Your device and browser extensions may have their own access to
      clipboard or page contents.
    </p>
    <h2>Guide comments</h2>
    <p>
      Guides have an optional comment form. When you post, we store the name and
      comment you enter, the guide it belongs to and the time. We do not store
      your IP address: a keyed fingerprint of it that changes every day is kept
      only to limit spam. Before posting, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that you
      are not a bot; its script loads only after you start writing a comment and
      is processed by Cloudflare under its policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting requests</h2>
    <p>
      Serving the website requires normal HTTP requests for pages and assets.
      The hosting provider may process technical request information such as IP
      addresses and request headers under its policies. Local development is
      served by your development machine; the deployment target is Cloudflare
      Static Assets.
    </p>
    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Guides may link to outside documentation. Those sites have separate data
      practices. Tool inputs are not included in these links.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      See <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> for the current support status. This
      policy must be reviewed when hosting, contact channels or third-party
      integrations change.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
